  "Question": "\\(4:5=x:20\\). What is \\(x\\)? Calculate: \\(4\\times20\\div5=?\\)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "16",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(5x=80\\), \\(x=16\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Scale both ratio terms\n\nMultiplying both terms of a ratio by the same nonzero number leaves its quotient unchanged. Since \\(20=5\\times4\\), multiply both terms of \\(4:5\\) by \\(4\\):\n\\[\n4:5=(4\\times4):(5\\times4)=16:20.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(x=16\\).",
